          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is window film worth it for Philadelphia weather?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Absolutely. Philadelphia's hot, humid summers drive up cooling costs—window film blocks up to 80% of solar heat before it enters your building, reducing AC load significantly. Our UV-blocking film works year-round to protect against sun damage (UV rays penetrate glass even in winter). Safety film provides storm protection during severe weather events common to the Delaware Valley."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Will window film make my rooms too dark?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Modern window films maintain natural light while reducing glare and heat. We offer a range of visible light transmission levels—from nearly clear UV-blocking film (80%+ light) to moderate tint (50% light) to darker privacy film (20% light). During your free consultation, we'll show samples and help you choose the right balance of light, heat rejection, and privacy for each room or exposure."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
